From: Rosen Penev <rosenp@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: b43: hold the frames of dozing stations as an AP

b43 does nothing when a station of its AP goes to sleep: sta_notify is
empty, and the PMQ of the firmware is disabled. mac80211 buffers the
frames for the station that it still holds, and takes back those that
fail while it dozes, but the frames already in tx_queue are sent to a
station that does not listen. Each A-MPDU frame among them is sent
B43_AMPDU_RETRY_LIMIT more times, and then dropped, as mac80211 frees
A-MPDU frames that come back filtered. Erik Conijn measured 46% ping
loss to a phone with its screen off under load on a Netgear R6400,
and none with his fix.

Like ath9k does, keep the frames in the driver while their station
dozes, as they are taken from tx_queue:
- give the plain ones back to mac80211 as filtered, so that it buffers
  them with the others, sets the TIM bit and sends them for a PS-Poll;
- hold the A-MPDU frames in a queue of the station, which keeps their
  place in the block ack window, and report their TIDs as buffered;
- send held frames for a PS-Poll or uAPSD trigger in
  release_buffered_frames, with More Data set while more are buffered
  and the end of the service period on the last one;
- put the held frames back at the head of tx_queue when the station
  wakes, ahead of what mac80211 buffered meanwhile.
Frames released for a trigger only join an A-MPDU with each other.

Nothing changes while no station dozes.

Based on "b43: AP mode: hold frames for stations in power save" by
Erik Conijn, adapted to frames taken from the mac80211 TXQs and to the
TX path running without wl->mutex.

Reported-by: Erik Conijn <egc112@msn.com>
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Rosen Penev <rosenp@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/b43.h
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/b43.h
@@ -853,6 +853,14 @@ struct b43_sta {
 	u16 baw_start[IEEE80211_NUM_TIDS];
 	/* MPDUs from baw_start sent and waiting for their final status */
 	u64 baw_pending[IEEE80211_NUM_TIDS];
+	/* AP mode: the station dozes */
+	bool asleep;
+	/* psq is set up, and frames may be added to it */
+	bool ps_init;
+	/* A-MPDU frames held while the station dozes, by their lock */
+	struct sk_buff_head psq;
+	/* TIDs of psq reported to mac80211 as buffered */
+	u16 ps_tids;
 };
 
